BioModels model files: CC0 1.0 Universal

This notice applies to the five downloaded SBML files:
  BIOMD0000000010.xml
  BIOMD0000000026.xml
  BIOMD0000000027.xml
  BIOMD0000000029.xml
  BIOMD0000000031.xml

BioModels dedicates its encoded models and associated annotations to the public
domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication.
These files are not relicensed under this fork's MIT license.

BioModels terms of use (checked 2026-11-07):
  https://biomodels.org/termsofuse
CC0 deed:
  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
CC0 legal code:
  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
BioModels team's published explanation of the policy:
  https://doi.org/10.1002/psp4.3

Evidence preserved in the exact downloaded files:
  0010 and 0027: explicit CC0 dedication in the model notes.
  0026: scientific model notes without an embedded license statement.
  0029 and 0031: historical BioModels copyright notices and terms-of-use links.
For the latter three, the CC0 designation is based on the BioModels repository
policy rather than a newly inserted statement in the XML.

Original scientific sources:
  Kholodenko BN (2000), doi:10.1046/j.1432-1327.2000.01197.x (model 0010).
  Markevich NI, Hoek JB, Kholodenko BN (2004), doi:10.1083/jcb.200308060
  (models 0026, 0027, 0029, 0031).

We retain model-author and BioModels attribution as scientific provenance.
The model files' original annotations and bytes are unchanged; SHA-256 hashes
and download URLs are recorded in manifest.json. CC0 for the encoded models
does not extend to the source papers, upstream MATLAB code or third-party tools.
